---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Photo from "../components/Photo.astro";
import { photo } from "../data/media";
import { siteConfig } from "../config/site";
---
<BaseLayout title="The concept | NIPO Japanese-Brazilian dining" description="Discover the Nipo-Brasileiro heritage behind NIPO: Japanese sushi craft, Brazilian fire and warm hospitality on Newcastle Quayside.">
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="concept-opening">
      <div class="concept-opening__copy" data-reveal><p class="label">Welcome to NIPO</p><h1>Two cultures.<br />One table.</h1><p class="lead">Japanese precision. Brazilian warmth.<br />Sushi, robata and dishes made for sharing.</p><a class="text-link" href="#heritage">The story behind NIPO <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
      <Photo asset={photo("fish-avocado-tartare")} eager sizes="(max-width:767px) 100vw, 50vw" />
    </section>
    <section class="heritage-section section-shell" id="heritage">
      <h2 data-reveal>The Nipo-Brasileiro connection</h2>
      <div class="editorial-copy" data-reveal>
        <p>NIPO takes its name from the Nipo-Brasileiro community of São Paulo, shaped by more than a century of Japanese migration to Brazil. That story began in 1908, when the Kasato Maru arrived at the port of Santos carrying Japanese migrants.</p>
        <p>Today, Brazil is home to the largest community of Japanese descent outside Japan, with São Paulo at the heart of that story. Across generations, families have brought their traditions into Brazilian life, creating a connection that continues to grow.</p>
        <p>That shared heritage inspires NIPO: Japanese precision, craft and restraint alongside Brazilian warmth, generosity and hospitality. Here on Newcastle Quayside, we bring those influences together through sushi, robata, bold flavours and dishes made for sharing.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="editorial-feature editorial-feature--ivory">
      <Photo asset={photo("salmon-sushi")} sizes="(max-width:767px) 100vw, 50vw" />
      <div class="editorial-feature__copy" data-reveal><h2>Care in every cut.</h2><p>Japanese craft gives our food its attention to detail: the cut of the fish, the balance of rice and the finish of each roll. Ingredients, texture and presentation all have a part to play.</p><p>For you, that means a menu to explore at your own pace. Begin with sushi and small plates, share a favourite and try something unfamiliar. Delicate flavours and bolder dishes each have a place at the table.</p></div>
    </section>
    <section class="editorial-feature editorial-feature--reverse">
      <Photo asset={photo("steak-salad")} sizes="(max-width:767px) 100vw, 50vw" />
      <div class="editorial-feature__copy" data-reveal><h2>Finished by fire.</h2><p>Robata brings the grill into the meal. Careful cooking over fire adds depth and char, alongside the bold flavours and generous spirit we take from Brazilian dining.</p><p>Choose a mix of sushi, skewers and steak to share, or follow your own favourites. The idea is simple: bring different tastes together in one meal, with something for everyone to discover.</p></div>
    </section>
    <section class="hospitality section-shell">
      <div data-reveal><h2>Why one table matters.</h2><p class="lead">Food has a way of bringing people closer.</p><p>We believe a shared meal creates room for curiosity and connection. Passing a plate, discovering a flavour and hearing the story behind it can turn dinner into something you remember together.</p><p>That is the purpose of NIPO: to celebrate this meeting of cultures through thoughtful food and a generous welcome. Settle in with a cocktail, make room for another dish and take your time. Our table is here to bring people together.</p><div class="action-row"><a class="button button--ivory" href="/menus/">Explore the menus</a><a class="text-link" href={siteConfig.bookingUrl}>Book a table <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div>
      <Photo asset={photo("botanical-cocktail")} sizes="(max-width:767px) 100vw, 40vw" />
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
